{{!
    @template local_moodesk/composer_send

    The reply composer's send control.

    An icon button, sitting to the right of the message box as one unit with it,
    the way a messaging app puts it. There is no action bar under the composer
    any more: with Cancel gone — the drawer's own close control is the way out of
    a ticket, and a second one inside the conversation was duplicating it — the
    only thing left to put there was this, and a whole strip for one button was
    height the conversation could have had.

    It is a real submit inside the moodleform, not a control that drives one.
    The form is submitted the same way it always was: natively on the canonical
    page, and intercepted by amd/src/reply_submit.js inside the drawer, which
    listens on the form's own submit event. Nothing here knows about either.

    Rendered into the form by \local_moodesk\form\reply_form, which owns the
    label — the composer sends a public reply or an internal note depending on
    which mode is selected, and amd/src/reply_toggle.js rewrites the label when
    the mode changes. The two labels travel on the element so the toggle has
    them without a second round trip for a string.

    Context variables:
      * label     - Accessible name for the current mode
      * replylabel - Accessible name while the composer is on Public Reply
      * notelabel - Accessible name while it is on Internal Note

    Example context (json):
    {
      "label": "Send reply",
      "replylabel": "Send reply",
      "notelabel": "Add internal note"
    }
}}
<button type="submit"
        class="mhd-composer__send"
        data-region="mhd-composer-send"
        data-label-reply="{{replylabel}}"
        data-label-note="{{notelabel}}"
        title="{{label}}"
        aria-label="{{label}}">
    <svg class="mhd-composer__send-icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <use href="#mhd-icon-send"></use>
    </svg>
</button>
